  "content": {
    "id": "p141-g24-27-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Which of the following satisfy $f(f(x))=x$?",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p141-g24-27-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Satisfies condition.",
          "worked": "The inner reciprocal requires $x\\ne0$. Its output is nonzero, so the second reciprocal is defined.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe condition holds for every $x$ in the domain of $f$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p141-g24-27-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Satisfies condition.",
          "worked": "The inner function requires $x\\ne1$. For these inputs, $f(x)-1=\\frac{1}{x-1}\\ne0$, so the second application is defined.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x-1}}{\\frac{x}{x-1}-1}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x-1}}{\\frac{1}{x-1}}\\\\f(f(x))&=x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe condition holds for every $x$ in the domain of $f$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p141-g24-27-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x-1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Does not satisfy condition.",
          "worked": "The inner function requires $x\\ne0$. The outer denominator also requires $f(x)\\ne0$, giving $x\\ne1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x-1}{x}-1}{\\frac{x-1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{-\\frac{1}{x}}{\\frac{x-1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=-\\frac{1}{x-1}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{1}{1-x}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis is not the identity function: at $x=2$, $f(f(2))=-1\\ne2$. The condition does not hold.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p141-g24-27-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Does not satisfy condition.",
          "worked": "The inner function requires $x\\ne0$. The outer denominator also requires $f(x)\\ne0$, giving $x\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x+1}{x}+1}{\\frac{x+1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{2x+1}{x}}{\\frac{x+1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{2x+1}{x+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis is not the identity function: at $x=1$, $f(f(1))=\\frac{3}{2}\\ne1$. The condition does not hold.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
